\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Self-preference bias in LLM-as-judge.} Faithfulness scores on four axes shift when the judge is swapped from Gemini\nobreakspace  {}3\nobreakspace  {}Flash (v1, same family as the agents' backbone) to Claude Sonnet\nobreakspace  {}4.5 (v2, non-family) on identical traces. The single-LLM \texttt  {llm\_control}'s lead over the scaffolded \texttt  {mdagents} shrinks on every axis and reverses on \emph  {depth} (3.10 vs.\ 3.49) --- the directionally expected signal for multi-expert debate. Judge-family is thus a first-class confound, not a free methodological choice.\relax }}{12}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig_selfpref}{{4}{12}{\textbf {Self-preference bias in LLM-as-judge.} Faithfulness scores on four axes shift when the judge is swapped from Gemini~3~Flash (v1, same family as the agents' backbone) to Claude Sonnet~4.5 (v2, non-family) on identical traces. The single-LLM \texttt {llm\_control}'s lead over the scaffolded \texttt {mdagents} shrinks on every axis and reverses on \emph {depth} (3.10 vs.\ 3.49) --- the directionally expected signal for multi-expert debate. Judge-family is thus a first-class confound, not a free methodological choice.\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
